@startuml request-async-actividad
!define USE_MOCHA
!include utils/theme.puml

!ifdef USE_MOCHA
  skinparam activity {
    BackgroundColor<<PRE>> CP_MOCHA_mauve
    FontColor<<PRE>> CP_MOCHA_base
    BackgroundColor<<POST>> CP_MOCHA_green
    FontColor<<POST>> CP_MOCHA_base
    BackgroundColor<<ERROR>> CP_MOCHA_red
    FontColor<<ERROR>> CP_MOCHA_base
    BackgroundColor<<SUCCESS>> CP_MOCHA_blue
    FontColor<<SUCCESS>> CP_MOCHA_base
  }
!else
  skinparam activity {
    BackgroundColor<<PRE>> CP_LATTE_mauve
    FontColor<<PRE>> CP_LATTE_base
    BackgroundColor<<POST>> CP_LATTE_green
    FontColor<<POST>> CP_LATTE_base
    BackgroundColor<<ERROR>> CP_LATTE_red
    FontColor<<ERROR>> CP_LATTE_base
    BackgroundColor<<SUCCESS>> CP_LATTE_blue
    FontColor<<SUCCESS>> CP_LATTE_base
  }
!endif

title Asynchronous Request Processing — Virtual Threads (Quartz removed)

|Client|
start
:**PRECONDITION**\n· POST /api/clients (create-client request)\n· CreateClientRequest body; <<PRE>>

|RequestService|
:submitClientCreateRequest(createClientRequest);
:Build Request\n(id=UUID, status=PENDING, requestData=JSON);
:RequestRepository.save(request)\n@Transactional — commits synchronously;
:**POSTCONDITION**\n· Request row committed with status=PENDING\n· caller does not wait for processing; <<POST>>

|Client|
:✔  HTTP 202 Accepted\n{ id, status: PENDING }; <<SUCCESS>>

|RequestService|
:Call requestProcessingService\n.processClientCreateRequest(id)\n(outside any transaction);

|RequestProcessingService|
:**PRECONDITION**\n· @Async method\n· spring.threads.virtual.enabled=true\n· no manual TaskExecutor bean\n  → Spring Boot autoconfigures\n    applicationTaskExecutor on virtual threads; <<PRE>>
:Dispatched on a virtual thread;
note right
  No Quartz in this flow. Quartz was removed from this project by
  architectural decision — it was being misused as a fire-once
  dispatcher instead of for its intended purpose (recurring /
  distributed scheduling).
end note
:RequestStateService.markProcessing(id);

|RequestStateService|
:Update Request.status = PROCESSING;

|RequestProcessingService|
:Deserialize CreateClientRequest\nfrom requestData;
:ClientService.create(createClientRequest);

if (business logic succeeded?) then (yes)
  :RequestStateService.markCompleted\n(id, ApiResult.ok(clientResponse));
  |RequestStateService|
  :Update Request.status = COMPLETED\n+ responseData = serialized result; <<SUCCESS>>
else (no)
  |RequestProcessingService|
  :✘  Catch exception inside the @Async method\n(never propagates to the caller); <<ERROR>>
  :RequestStateService.markFailed\n(id, ApiResult.error(...));
  |RequestStateService|
  :Update Request.status = FAILED\n+ responseData = error payload; <<ERROR>>
endif
:**POSTCONDITION**\n· Request reaches a terminal state\n  (COMPLETED or FAILED)\n· exception handling fully encapsulated\n  inside the async method; <<POST>>

|Client|
:Poll GET /api/requests/{id};

|RequestResource|
:RequestService.getRequestStatus(id);
if (Request found?) then (no)
  :✘  RequestNotFoundException → HTTP 404; <<ERROR>>
  kill
else (yes)
endif
:Return RequestStatusResponse\n(id, type, status, timestamps, responseData);

|Client|
if (status == PENDING or PROCESSING?) then (yes)
  :Poll again after a delay;
  detach
else (COMPLETED / FAILED)
  :✔  Render final result; <<SUCCESS>>
  stop
endif

@enduml
